# Phase 13 – Search, Analytics & Statistics

This phase implements typo-tolerant course and card search workflows and detailed progress/Leitner statistics visualization on the mobile client.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Typo-Tolerant Search Logic:** The search will be executed fully offline on the client. We will implement a custom Levenshtein distance algorithm in a clean helper utility. Query terms of length 3–4 will tolerate up to 1 typo, and longer terms will tolerate up to 2 typos.
>
> **Safety Confirmation Dialog:** In compliance with Phase 10/11 requirements, when a user selects a card from search results, if that card is currently in Leitner Boxes 2–5, the application will show a confirmation dialog warning that viewing it directly will reset its learning progress back to Box 1. If confirmed, its progress is reset and the card is opened. Box 1 and Box 6 (Finished) cards open directly without prompting.
>
> **My Courses Toggle:** We will add a TabBar/SegmentedControl at the top of the existing `CoursesScreen` to let users toggle between "Catalog" (all courses) and "My Courses" (downloaded/purchased only), integrating the "My Courses" view directly into the Course tab.

## Open Questions

> [!NOTE]
> **Server-side Analytics:** Currently, Phase 13 requirements do not specify any new server-side reporting APIs. All analytics and statistics are computed locally from the client SQLite databases (`courses_cache` and `client_progress`), matching the offline-first requirement. Please confirm if any server-side analytics report uploads are required beyond the existing sync endpoint.

